# React components

- Functional components only; `const` arrow components with named exports
- Keep components focused; extract complex logic into `use*` hooks
- Props via interfaces; avoid prop drilling beyond ~2 levels
- Do not call hooks conditionally
- Prefer composition over deep prop trees

```typescript
interface ButtonProps {
  label: string;
  onClick: () => void;
  variant?: "primary" | "secondary";
  disabled?: boolean;
}

export const Button = ({
  label,
  onClick,
  variant = "primary",
  disabled = false,
}: ButtonProps) => {
  return (
    <button className={`btn btn-${variant}`} onClick={onClick} disabled={disabled}>
      {label}
    </button>
  );
};
```

## Performance

- Lazy-load heavy routes/components
- Virtualize long lists
- Wrap feature sections with error boundaries and meaningful fallbacks
- Do not add `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default; only when measuring a real need
